{"commit":{"committer":{"date":"2026-11-20T21:45:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Enroll System.IO.Compression and its tests in unsafe-v2 (#136657)\n\n\u003c!-- --\u003e\n\nI chose `System.IO.Compression` (and its tests) as the first target\nbecause it's relatively small and interop-heavy.\n\nThis PR covers only the mechanical migration: there is no AI-driven work\nto fill in safety comments or decide which methods might need a\ncaller-unsafe contract. This lets the review focus entirely on the code\nfixer output.\n\n## References\n\n- Unsafe-v2 spec:\n[link](https://github.com/dotnet/csharplang/blob/main/proposals/unsafe-evolution.md)\n- Order of operations:\n[link](https://gist.github.com/EgorBo/1ed6752b3430a181240dcee7dace7070)\n([tracking issue](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/issues/131451))\n- Driver script (runs the fixers in the correct order):\n[link](https://gist.github.com/EgorBo/456f9e7d3680a5f9c8e54a168a907187)\n\nA prompt for reading all the relevant documentation and running the\ndriver script:\n\n```\nRead https://gist.githubusercontent.com/EgorBo/271abeeac2bfb5a34013e4562507062e/raw/unsafe-v2-migration-agent-prompt.md in full\nand follow it for **System.IO.Compression** and its tests. Run the driver once per project.\n```\n\n_(I also tell it where to find a prebuilt dotnet/runtime in WSL so it\ncan handle Linux targets there.)_\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot \u003c223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com\u003e\nCopilot-Session: 5d9d8def-16fe-4105-9e0f-b8aad187abce\nCopilot-Session: 9190ec1a-b880-4650-942f-d7f17a4d06f8"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/commit/1078913f561abffd961345666c3126b42f4afc68","sha":"1078913f561abffd961345666c3126b42f4afc68"}
